  "n_predictors": 2,
  "predictive_utility": 0.5,
  "rationale": "Both added columns are genuine content-derived predictors that capture specific negative service experiences (inattention, rudeness) known drivers of low Yelp satisfaction. They are not restatements, components, or leakage of label_pos, and each plausibly carries signal. However, they are correlated with each other, cover only a narrow slice of possible dissatisfaction drivers (e.g., food quality, price, wait time, cleanliness are absent), and are relatively sparse (~37-38 positives of 250), giving moderate rather than strong incremental predictive leverage over the raw review_text."
}
